# Joey Agent — line-ending policy.
#
# This repo embeds text assets into binaries with include_str! and asserts
# on exact LF-terminated content (speckit bodies, prompt baselines,
# fixtures). core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites them to CRLF in the
# worktree, corrupting byte-parity tests. Force LF in worktree AND index
# for those assets. Everything else stays text=auto (local preference).

# Embedded workflow bodies — parsed with LF-only frontmatter delimiters.
crates/joey-cli/src/speckit_bodies/** text eol=lf

# Prompt parity baselines compared byte-for-byte after line filtering.
specs/**/baseline/*.txt text eol=lf

# Shell scripts executed via bash (LF required).
*.sh text eol=lf
.specify/scripts/** text eol=lf

# Rust and standard source: normalize to LF in index; worktree follows
# local autocrlf EXCEPT nothing here depends on CRLF, so keep uniform LF
# to avoid mixed-ending files.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
